-- int-wiring.l4: the standard inputs of PLAN section (c), wired from the group that decides each to the groups that read it.  One function per integration point (or per group of them),
-- named for the standard `GIVEN` it produces, and nothing here decides a question of the Law: every rule called is a rule of one of the nine groups, and every discretion remains an input.
-- Where the PLAN's input name and the encoder's actual exported name differ, the encoder's file governs (assignment of the integrator).

§ `Integration layer -- wiring the standard inputs (PLAN section (c))`

§§ `IP19, IP34: the required steps notices served`

-- IP34: the date on which a notice is served, fixed by group G7 (Article 38) from the dates sent and received and from any Order.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      notice IS A `Notice served in the case` @desc The notice
GIVETH A DATE
`Int IP34 the date on which the notice was served` readings notice MEANS
    `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (notice's `date sent`) (notice's `date received`) (notice's `date fixed by an Order under Article 38`)
        (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)

-- IP19: one record per service, made by group G8 (Article 27(2)) with the date of service of IP34.
-- IP34 for a notice of a decision (a deregistration, a decision appealed): the date on which it was served, fixed by group G7 (Article 38).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      notice IS A `Notice of a decision in the case` @desc The notice of the decision
GIVETH A DATE
`Int IP34 the date on which the notice of a decision was served` readings notice MEANS
    `Art 38 the date on which the notice is served` (notice's `date sent`) (notice's `date received`) (notice's `date fixed by an Order under Article 38`)
        (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)

GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      notice IS A `Notice served in the case` @desc The notice
GIVETH A `Required steps notice`
`Int IP19 the required steps notice` readings notice MEANS
    `Art 27(2) the required steps notice served` (readings's `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) (notice's recipient) (notice's belief)
        (`Int IP34 the date on which the notice was served` readings notice) (notice's time) (notice's requirements) (notice's `the steps required have been taken`)

GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      notices IS A LIST OF `Notice served in the case` @desc The notices served
GIVETH A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
`Int IP19 the required steps notices served` readings notices MEANS
    map (GIVEN n YIELD `Int IP19 the required steps notice` readings n) notices

§§ `IP5, IP21: the entity, its kinds, its Jersey-entity status and its governors with their reportable matters`

-- One governor, with the reportable matters group G6 finds (Article 19(1)); the name and the other facts are the person's own.
GIVEN governor IS A Governor @desc The person's record from group G1
      matters IS A LIST OF `Kind of reportable matter` @desc The kinds of reportable matter that describe the person (IP21)
GIVETH A Governor
`Int the governor with the reportable matters` governor matters MEANS
    Governor WITH
        name IS governor's name
        `is a natural person` IS governor's `is a natural person`
        `is resident in Jersey` IS governor's `is resident in Jersey`
        `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS governor's `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)`
        `reportable matters` IS matters

-- The kinds of entity (IP5, Article 2(1)).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law in force
      body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The body
GIVETH A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
`Int IP5 the kinds of entity` readings vintage body MEANS
    `Art 2(1) the kinds of entity the body falls within` (readings's `reading of Articles 1 and 2`) vintage (body's facts)

-- The people who are governors (Article 2(7)), in the order given.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law in force
      body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The body
GIVETH A LIST OF `Person in the case`
`Int the people who are governors` readings vintage body MEANS
    filter (GIVEN p YIELD `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` (readings's `reading of Articles 1 and 2`) (`Int IP5 the kinds of entity` readings vintage body) (body's model) (p's considered's role)) (body's people)

-- IP21: one governor with the reportable matters found by group G6 (Article 19(1)).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      notices IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice` @desc IP19: the required steps notices served
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      p IS A `Person in the case` @desc The person, who is a governor
GIVETH A Governor
`Int IP21 the governor with the reportable matters found` readings notices day p MEANS
    `Int the governor with the reportable matters` (p's considered's person) (`Art 19(1) the reportable matters of the person` (readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) notices day (p's `facts for the reportable matters`))

-- IP21: the governors, each with the reportable matters found by group G6.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law in force
      notices IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice` @desc IP19: the required steps notices served
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The body
GIVETH A LIST OF Governor
`Int IP21 the governors with their reportable matters` readings vintage notices day body MEANS
    map (GIVEN p YIELD `Int IP21 the governor with the reportable matters found` readings notices day p) (`Int the people who are governors` readings vintage body)

-- IP5: the entity as Article 2 leaves it. The facts G1 reads for Article 2(3)(b)(ii) carry the same governors.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law in force
      notices IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice` @desc IP19: the required steps notices served
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The body
GIVETH AN Entity
`Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day body MEANS
    `Art 2 the body as an entity` (readings's `reading of Articles 1 and 2`) vintage (body's name) (body's standing)
        (map (GIVEN u YIELD u's purpose) (body's purposes))
        (`Int the facts about the body with the governors` (body's facts) (`Int IP21 the governors with their reportable matters` readings vintage notices day body))

-- IP6: whether the entity is a registered charity, by group G1 (Article 1).
GIVEN entity IS AN Entity @desc The entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity MEANS
    `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` entity

§§ `IP3, IP8 to IP11: the Minister's office, the charity test, the same fact at two times, the Order that carries it, the advancement of religion`

-- IP3: the office that "Minister" names in the text of the Law (group G1). It is lazy: a reading of Article 5(2) that does not read the office never forces it.
GIVEN vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law in force
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`Int IP3 the office of the Minister` vintage MEANS
    `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` vintage

-- IP8: whether the entity meets the charity test (group G2, Article 5). The purposes the test reads are the entity's own purposes, with the facts Article 6(2) reads about each.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law in force
      entity IS AN Entity @desc The entity (IP5)
      purposes IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` @desc The entity's purposes with the facts Article 6(2) reads about each
      facts IS A `Facts for the charity test in the case` @desc The facts the charity test reads apart from the purposes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP8 the entity meets the charity test` readings vintage entity purposes facts MEANS
    `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` (readings's `reading of Articles 3 to 7`) entity purposes (facts's `constitution facts`) (`Int IP3 the office of the Minister` vintage)
        (facts's `public benefit determination`) (facts's `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies Article 5(2) for the entity`)

-- IP10: whether the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3) (group G2), which Article 8(3)(i) asks of the register.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law in force
      entity IS AN Entity @desc The entity (IP5)
      purposes IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads` @desc The entity's purposes with the facts Article 6(2) reads about each
      facts IS A `Facts for the charity test in the case` @desc The facts the charity test reads apart from the purposes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP10 the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` readings vintage entity purposes facts MEANS
    `Art 5(3) the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` (readings's `reading of Articles 3 to 7`) entity purposes (facts's `constitution facts`) (`Int IP3 the office of the Minister` vintage)
        (facts's `public benefit determination`) (facts's `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies Article 5(2) for the entity`)

-- IP11: whether the entity has a purpose within Article 6(1)(c) itself (group G2), which Article 28(1)(a) reads.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      entity IS AN Entity @desc The entity (IP5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP11 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` readings entity MEANS
    `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` (readings's `reading of Articles 3 to 7`) entity

§§ `IP17, IP18, IP22 to IP24: the principal address, the name, the declarations, the bar on granting and the court's order`

-- IP17: whether the entity has a principal address in Jersey (group G3, Article 8(4)).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      entity IS AN Entity @desc The entity (IP5)
      facts IS A `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` @desc The facts Article 8(4) reads
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP17 the entity has a principal address in Jersey` readings entity facts MEANS
    `Art 8(4) the entity has a principal address in Jersey` (readings's `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) entity facts

-- IP18: whether a name is undesirable (group G4, Article 12(1); the Commissioner's opinion is the input).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      opinion IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The Commissioner's opinion on the name
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP18 the name is undesirable` readings opinion MEANS
    `Art 12(1) the name is undesirable` (readings's `reading of Articles 11 and 12`) opinion

-- The position of each governor for Article 19(5), read from the people of the case.
GIVEN people IS A LIST OF `Person in the case` @desc The people who are governors
GIVETH A LIST OF `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)`
`Int the positions of the governors for Article 19(5)` people MEANS
    map (GIVEN p YIELD `Position of a governor for Article 19(5)` OF (p's considered's person's name), (p's `made a report under paragraph (2)`), (p's `provided a declaration of no reportable matter`)) people

-- IP22: whether the applicant has complied with Article 19(5) (group G6).
GIVEN stated IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application states that the entity holds declarations from all its governors who have not made a report
      people IS A LIST OF `Person in the case` @desc The people who are governors
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP22 the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)` stated people MEANS
    `Art 19(5) the applicant has stated that it holds declarations from all its governors who have not reported` stated (`Int the positions of the governors for Article 19(5)` people)

-- IP23: whether Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application (group G6): a reported matter about a governor is undetermined, or its resulting order or notice has not been complied with.
GIVEN people IS A LIST OF `Person in the case` @desc The people who are governors
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP23 Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` people MEANS
    `Art 19(9)(c) bars granting the application` (catMaybes (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `reported matter awaiting determination`) people))

-- IP24: whether the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered (group G6, Article 20(1)(c)).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      orders IS A LIST OF `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` @desc The orders the court has made under Article 20(1)
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP24 the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered` readings orders day MEANS
    `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` (readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) orders day

§§ `IP29: an Order under Article 13(9), read limb by limb`

-- Group G5 produces one fact, "an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity", TRUE if the Order requires or provides anything (payment details (a), a statement of intentions (b), entry on the register (c)) and no
-- relief Order disapplies it. Group G4 reads it for limb (b) only (Article 11(2)(e)(ii)) and group G3 for limb (c) only (Article 8(3)(m)). The integration layer wires each consumer from the limb it reads (see NOTES.md, IP29).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      order IS A MAYBE `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc The Order under Article 13(9); NOTHING if there is none
      reliefs IS A LIST OF `Order under Article 13(10)` @desc The relief Orders under Article 13(10)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP29 the composite fact of group G5` readings order reliefs MEANS
    `Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` (readings's `reading of Articles 13 and 14`) order reliefs

GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      order IS A MAYBE `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc The Order under Article 13(9); NOTHING if there is none
      reliefs IS A LIST OF `Order under Article 13(10)` @desc The relief Orders under Article 13(10)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies` readings order reliefs MEANS
    CONSIDER order
      WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
      WHEN JUST theOrder THEN
            theOrder's `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)`
        AND NOT `Art 13(10) a relief Order disapplies an Order under paragraph (9) for the charity` (readings's `reading of Articles 13 and 14`) reliefs

GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      order IS A MAYBE `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc The Order under Article 13(9); NOTHING if there is none
      reliefs IS A LIST OF `Order under Article 13(10)` @desc The relief Orders under Article 13(10)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int IP29 an Order under Article 13(9)(c) applies` readings order reliefs MEANS
    CONSIDER order
      WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
      WHEN JUST theOrder THEN
            theOrder's `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)`
        AND NOT `Art 13(10) a relief Order disapplies an Order under paragraph (9) for the charity` (readings's `reading of Articles 13 and 14`) reliefs
